Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||04-24-2000||08:12 PM||||I just got my 1" Addco swaybar and was wondering if anyone has removed/installed the rear swaybar on an 88. Does the cradle need to be lowered to get it in there? I could go look, but why get all dirty when I can ask you guys  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>BTW, this bar is very nice looking... too bad it's gonna be hiden up under the car <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||04-24-2000||09:58 PM||||Two questions: <BR>1.) What is the stock sway bar size on an 88?<BR>2.) Where did you find a aftermarket bar for an 88?<BR>Thanks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||04-24-2000||10:13 PM||||The stock 88 bar is 7/8". <P>I got my bar from a person that bought it from Ryane and decided not to use it. I priced the complete setup from Ryane at $253 including all brackets needed to add it to a Fiero that never had one. $63 for the brackets. I got that complete setup for $155. The bar is an Addco and even came with 4 cool stickers and complete poly bushings in the end-links and saddles.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||04-24-2000||10:16 PM||||I've pulled the stock rear sway bar out of my Formula twice. both times I pulled it when the cradle was already lowered. I don't think you can put it in without lowering the cradle several inches. The ends where the endlinks connect won't go through such a narrow opening as I recall.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||04-25-2000||12:13 AM||||I just removed a rear sway bar from a Formula 5-sp. without droppng the cradle, so it can be done.  I imagine it would be impossible with the larger (longer) auto. tranny. ||||reg||3
